.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Hendrik Casimir showed in 1948 that two uncharged, perfectly conducting parallel plates in vacuum should attract each other: only electromagnetic vacuum modes that fit an integer number of wavelengths between the plates are allowed there, so the confined zero-point energy is slightly lower than in the unbounded vacuum outside, producing a net inward force. This is a simplified, standard textbook treatment -- a 1D scalar field confined between two &quot;plates&quot; a distance d apart, not a full 3D electromagnetic calculation. casimir_mode_frequencies builds the resulting discrete standing-wave spectrum,">

